00:03:50.077 --> 00:03:54.837
Worth keeping an eye on, astronomers and rival operators argue the star-mind constellation

00:03:54.837 --> 00:03:59.897
will increase orbital debris risk, radio frequency interference, and light pollution that

00:03:59.897 --> 00:04:02.337
degrades both optical and radio observations.

00:04:02.337 --> 00:04:08.177
Those objections are the reason the FCC order limits the license to backup KABAN radio

00:04:08.177 --> 00:04:14.397
links and requires an accepted debris mitigation plan before any satellite flies above 600 km.

00:04:15.157 --> 00:04:20.477
Amazon called the timeline and the size technically and economically unrealistic, and the order

00:04:20.477 --> 00:04:25.397
drops the financial surety bond that usually backstops debris risk while leaving the deployment

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:26.417
deadlines in force.

00:04:27.309 --> 00:04:32.649
For a star mine spacecraft, the engineering reality is a trade of radiator area and shielding

00:04:32.649 --> 00:04:36.389
mass against the land, water, and grid a ground hall has to buy.

00:04:36.949 --> 00:04:41.689
A satellite in those shells sees sunlight for nearly the entire orbit except brief eclipse

00:04:41.689 --> 00:04:46.909
periods, which removes the grid-scale battery or gas turbine buffering terrestrial facilities

00:04:46.909 --> 00:04:48.009
need at peak demand.

00:04:48.769 --> 00:04:53.909
Waste heat leaves through large radiator surfaces rather than evaporative cooling towers or chillers,

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:59.389
and the reported 75-meter wingspan and 30-meter deployed height supply the area for that

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:00.369
radiation balance.

00:05:00.369 --> 00:05:06.389
Heat dumped into space rises steeply as the surface warms, so that extra area lets processors

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:11.409
run at higher power density than air or water loops allow, holding junction temperatures

00:05:11.409 --> 00:05:14.649
within commercial grade limits without active refrigeration.

00:05:15.209 --> 00:05:20.229
Chips still take a slow radiation soak and sudden bit flips from trapped protons and electrons,

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:25.989
so the design adds aluminum or tantalum shielding or uses silicon on insulator processes.

00:05:25.989 --> 00:05:31.249
Chips built on an insulating layer that raised per die cost but cut upset rates.

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:36.489
Raw metal for that shielding costs far less than the finished package die, which is the

00:05:36.489 --> 00:05:41.809
gap the idiot index measures, how many times delivered compute costs over the silicon, metal

00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:43.249
and kilowatt hours inside.

00:05:43.989 --> 00:05:49.009
That index can fall if starship launch cost per kilogram drops enough to offset radiator

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:53.929
and shielding mass, compared with terrestrial sites that also pay for land, water rights,

00:05:53.929 --> 00:05:55.369
and grid interconnection.

00:05:55.709 --> 00:06:00.269
Day-to-day traffic rides optical inter-satellite links already flying on Starlink,

00:06:00.609 --> 00:06:06.009
so the radio path stays a narrow backup and any detected interference takes that channel offline,

00:06:06.589 --> 00:06:09.109
shifting reliability onto those optical terminals.

00:06:09.689 --> 00:06:14.929
The same architecture also frees site selection from fights over where to put a power plant on the ground.

00:06:15.529 --> 00:06:18.269
The plan is to start small in 2027,

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:23.309
increased through 2028 and hit very large volume in 2029,

00:06:23.309 --> 00:06:28.589
line, one starship flight rate and payload capacity stabilize, moving the bottleneck from

00:06:28.589 --> 00:06:31.169
silicon fabrication to assembly at gigabay.

00:06:31.709 --> 00:06:37.169
Filling incremental planes rather than requiring simultaneous global coverage cuts peak manufacturing

00:06:37.169 --> 00:06:42.129
load, the same staged method that grew starling from hundreds of spacecraft to more than

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:44.409
11,000 without ever halting service.

